    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> rvolosatovs created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15027#discussion_r4392096742\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>nit; could we use <code>saturating_add</code>?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 635479412,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793125809
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> rvolosatovs created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15027#discussion_r4392593820\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Could we split this in at least two frames instead to test that the <code>BodyWithPrefix</code> actually forwards to the wrapped <code>body</code> correctly?</p>\n<p>In the current test <code>BodyWithPrefix</code> never reads anything from the inner <code>body</code>, because it's read in full by <code>HostBodyStreamProducer</code>.</p>\n<p>We could also consider adding trailers here</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 635479413,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793125809
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> rvolosatovs created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15027#discussion_r4392090736\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>What do you think about storing <code>Bytes</code> directly and checking for <code>is_empty()</code> instead of <code>None</code>?</p>\n</blockquote>",
